    "answer": "Chronic stress can negatively impact sleep quality by contributing to symptoms such as anxiety, worry, and feeling overwhelmed, which may make it difficult to fall asleep or stay asleep. Since adults need 7-9 hours of sleep in cycles including REM and non-REM stages, consistently getting only 5 hours of sleep deprives the body of sufficient restorative sleep. This can lead to fatigue, difficulty concentrating, irritability, and increased feelings of being overwhelmed, thereby impairing overall mental wellness."
